---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://akturesult.bond";
const pageUrl = `${siteUrl}/guides/aktu-grading-system`;

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "@id": pageUrl,
      "url": pageUrl,
      "headline": "AKTU Grading System: 10-Point CBCS Scale, Passing Marks & Grace Rules",
      "description": "Complete breakdown of the AKTU Choice Based Credit System (CBCS) 10-point scale, minimum 30% external passing marks, 40% aggregate rules, and grace policies.",
      "datePublished": "2026-03-25T08:00:00+05:30",
      "dateModified": "2026-10-16T12:00:00+05:30",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond Student Editorial Team"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond",
        "url": siteUrl
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": `${pageUrl}/#breadcrumb`,
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": siteUrl },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Guides", "item": `${siteUrl}/guides` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Grading System", "item": pageUrl }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout 
  title="AKTU Grading System: 10-Point Scale, Passing Marks & Grace Rules | akturesult.bond"
  description="Master the AKTU CBCS grading scale. Learn passing thresholds (30% external, 40% aggregate), grace marks criteria (PWG), and letter grade mappings."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-black light:bg-white text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      
      <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-gray-300 light:text-gray-800 font-semibold truncate">Grading System</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border pb-6 mb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-brand-blue font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
          <span>Academic Ordinance</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>6 min read</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Updated October 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white light:text-ink leading-tight">
          AKTU Grading System: 10-Point CBCS Scale &amp; Passing Criteria
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          How do raw examination scores translate into letter grades and grade points under AKTU regulations? Here is the complete breakdown of minimum passing marks, aggregate rules, and grace policies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Mandatory Non-Affiliation Alert -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
        <strong>Important Student Notice:</strong> akturesult.bond is an independent student utility platform and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially connected to Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University (AKTU). This guide summarizes official university examination regulations.
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            1. Two Essential Passing Conditions in AKTU
          </h2>
          <p>
            To pass any credit theory subject in an AKTU semester exam, a student must simultaneously satisfy <strong>two mandatory conditions</strong>:
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-blue/30 bg-brand-blue/10 space-y-2">
              <strong class="text-brand-blue text-sm block">Condition 1: External Exam Minimum (30%)</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
                You must secure at least <strong>30% marks in the university end-semester written exam</strong>. For a 70-mark paper, you need at least <strong>21 marks</strong>. For a 100-mark paper, you need at least <strong>30 marks</strong>. Scoring below this triggers an automatic fail ('F' grade) regardless of internal marks.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/10 space-y-2">
              <strong class="text-emerald-400 text-sm block">Condition 2: Combined Aggregate Minimum (40%)</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
                Your combined total (Internal Sessional + External Exam) must be at least <strong>40% of the maximum marks</strong>. For a 100-mark total course (30 internal + 70 external), you must score at least <strong>40 total marks</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            2. The 10-Point Letter Grading Scale
          </h2>
          <p>
            Under the Choice Based Credit System (CBCS), grades reflect both academic mastery and relative ranking:
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-canvas-dark-surface light:bg-canvas-light-surface text-white light:text-ink">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Marks Range (%)</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Letter Grade</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Grade Point</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Qualitative Meaning</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-canvas-dark-border/40 light:divide-canvas-light-border font-mono">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">90% and above</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">O</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Outstanding</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">80% to 89%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">A+</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">9</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Excellent</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">70% to 79%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">A</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">8</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Very Good</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">65% to 69%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">B+</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">7</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Good</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">60% to 64%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-blue-400">B</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">6</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Above Average</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">50% to 59%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-amber-400">C</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">5</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Average</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3">40% to 49%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-amber-400">P</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold">4</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans">Pass</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 text-red-400">Below 40%</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">F</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">0</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-sans text-red-400">Fail / Back Paper</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            3. AKTU Grace Marks Policy (PWG - Passed With Grace)
          </h2>
          <p>
            To prevent students from losing an entire academic year due to marginal deficits in 1 or 2 subjects, AKTU awards grace marks under strict conditions:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Maximum Grace Quota:</strong> A maximum of <strong>up to 7 marks</strong> (or 10 marks depending on course ordinance) can be awarded across an academic year.</li>
            <li><strong>Full Clearance Requirement:</strong> Grace marks are only granted if the addition of those marks enables the student to pass all subjects in that academic year. Grace will NOT be awarded if the student still has outstanding back papers.</li>
            <li><strong>No Division Elevation:</strong> Grace marks cannot be added to improve overall percentage or elevate division from 2nd to 1st.</li>
            <li><strong>Status Tag:</strong> Marksheets receiving grace display the result status <strong>PWG</strong> (Passed With Grace) rather than regular PASS.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </div>

      <!-- Quick CTA -->
      <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue/20 to-purple-600/15 border border-brand-blue/30 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Facing a back paper?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600">Read our complete guide to Carry-Over Paper (COP) rules and year back avoidance.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/guides/aktu-carry-over-cop-back-paper" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-brand-blue hover:bg-brand-blue-hover text-white text-xs font-bold transition-all shadow-md shrink-0">
          Carry-Over (COP) Rules &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
